The textures in mixins/firstpersonmodel/sprites.rs are TRender's own
(src/main/resources/assets/trender/textures, MIT), converted to pixels by
tools/sprites.mjs; data/icon.png is First-person Model's icon. The panel, tab
and scroll bar textures are drawn as the plain fills they are.

This port rewrites First-person Model's logic (LogicHandler, its settings,
the toggle key) and the effect of its mixins in Rust for Horizon's native mod
API, and redraws its TRender config screen as TRender draws it. Changes from
the original: the body is drawn by drawing Horizon's own player model a second
time from a camera moved the other way, instead of extracting the camera
entity moved; no API for other mods (PlayerAnimator, Freecam support); the
"Auto Vanilla Hands" tab writes the list it shows (the original writes the
"Disable Items" list there); a hidden layer is hidden only on your own body,
not on other players drawn by the same renderer; the fishing line leaves the
body's hand moved with the body. Not Enough Animations is not part of this
port. It is not affiliated with tr7zw, Mojang or Microsoft.
